\begin_layout Standard
In order to better understand this section,
 let us recall that the Mandelbrot set is
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathbb{M}=\left\{ c\in\mathbb{C}|\,\,o(0,q_{c})\,\,\mathrm{is\,bounded}\right\} =\left\{ c\in\mathbb{C}|\,\,J(q_{c})\,\,\mathrm{is\,connected}\right\} ,
\]

\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $q_{c}(z)=z^{2}+c$
\end_inset

.
 The point 
\begin_inset Formula $0$
\end_inset

 is the critical point of each function 
\begin_inset Formula $q_{c}$
\end_inset

.
 The classical algorithm of coloring by escape time is commonly used to draw the Mandelbrot set (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:TheMandelbrot"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

