\begin_layout Standard
The bulbs of period 
\begin_inset Formula $N$
\end_inset

 of the Mandelbrot set are the open subsets 
\begin_inset Formula $U\subset\mathbb{M}$
\end_inset

 such that for every 
\begin_inset Formula $c\in U$
\end_inset

 the corresponding function 
\begin_inset Formula $q_{c}$
\end_inset

 has a finite attracting periodic orbit of period 
\begin_inset Formula $N$
\end_inset

,
 and it is known that the critical point 
\begin_inset Formula $0$
\end_inset

 belongs to the immediate basin of attraction of the orbit.
 The algorithm to draw these bulbs of period 
\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $2$
\end_inset

 use that 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{C}$
\end_inset

 is a complete metric space and the convergence of Cauchy sequences:
 the iteration is stopped when 
\begin_inset Formula $|q_{c}^{n}(0)-q_{c}^{n+2}(0)|<\varepsilon$
\end_inset

 and the points are coloring according to 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

.
 See 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:TheMandelbrot2"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
